course: dictionary
lesson: 11914
title: Burly: big and strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A burly person is big, strong and heavily built. Burly is an adjective, a describing word, so it tells you about a noun such as a person. One word gives you a picture of size and strength.
explain: «The burly guard lifted the heavy gate with one hand.» The guard lifts a heavy gate with one hand, so he must be strong. Burly must mean big and strong. Try it: swap in big and strong, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Burly is about strength and size, not about being fat. «The burly blacksmith hammered the hot iron into shape.» Hammering iron takes a powerful body, so the picture is of strength.
fact: Burly is an adjective: burly, burlier, burliest.
fact: «Burly» means big, strong and heavily built.
fact: In stories, burly men are often guards, policemen, sailors or blacksmiths.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the policemen who arrest Toad are burly.
fact: Burly describes a strong, solid body. It is not the same as fat.
exercise: «The burly guard lifted the heavy gate with one hand.» What does burly mean? | Loud and angry | Small and quick | Tired and hungry | *Big and strong
exercise: «The burly sailor pulled the rope all day without stopping.» Which word from the sentence tells you the sailor is strong? | day | rope | sailor | *pulled
exercise: Which person is burly? | A quiet cat asleep on a mat | *A big, strong man who lifts heavy boxes | A thin girl who runs very fast | A tiny child who is always sleepy
test: What does burly mean? | *Big, strong and heavily built | Quiet and shy | Tiny and thin | Slow and sleepy
test: Is burly the same as fat? | Yes, burly always means fat | Yes, burly means happy | Burly is a kind of animal | *No, burly means big and strong, not fat
exam: Which sentence uses burly correctly? | Burly is the name of a river that runs to the sea | *The burly builder carried the bricks up the ladder | The burly rain fell softly on the roof | Burly means running very fast
